{"task_id": "HumanEval/39", "solution": "def prime_fib(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    prime_fib returns n-th number that is a Fibonacci number and it's also prime.\n    >>> prime_fib(1)\n    2\n    >>> prime_fib(2)\n    3\n    >>> prime_fib(3)\n    5\n    >>> prime_fib(4)\n    13\n    >>> prime_fib(5)\n    89\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # is_prime checks if a given integer is a prime number.\n    def is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        if num == 2:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 3\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 2\n        return True\n\n    prime_fib_count = 0\n    a, b = 0, 1  # Initialize the first two Fibonacci numbers.\n\n    while True:\n        fib_number = a\n        a, b = b, a + b  # Generate the next Fibonacci number in sequence.\n\n        # Skip numbers less than 2 as they are not prime.\n        if fib_number < 2:\n            continue\n\n        if is_prime(fib_number):\n            prime_fib_count += 1\n            if prime_fib_count == n:\n                return fib_number"}
