{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "import math\ndef closest_integer(value: str) -> int:\n    '''\n    Create a function that takes a value (string) representing a number\n    and returns the closest integer to it. If equidistant, round away from zero.\n    '''\n    num = float(value)\n\n    floor_num = math.floor(num)\n    ceil_num = math.ceil(num)\n\n    diff_to_floor = abs(num - floor_num)\n    diff_to_ceil = abs(num - ceil_num)\n\n    if diff_to_floor == diff_to_ceil:\n        # Equidistant values are rounded away from zero.\n        # For X.5, if positive return ceil, if negative return floor.\n        if num >= 0:\n            return int(ceil_num)\n        else: # num < 0\n            return int(floor_num)\n    elif diff_to_floor < diff_to_ceil:\n        return int(floor_num)\n    else: # diff_to_ceil < diff_to_floor\n        return int(ceil_num)"}
